From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 04:22:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Range views draw nothing past their reach

A panorama's pixels read its range as a distance from the camera
(merge_spherical.frag), and what lies past it reads nothing; its side
cameras' frusta end at a flat far plane, so their corners reached 1.7
times as far. Panoramas (Lidar, RangeFinder: spherical or cylindrical)
now discard fragments past their range (encode_depth.frag) and skip
instances, and cells of them, wholly past it from the eye
(wr_camera_set_reach). The discarded fragments leave the background a
culled instance would, so the cull is exact: a forest flight's
/lidar/points are byte-identical with it off (IRONLARK_RANGE_REACH=0)
and on, over the whole of its deterministic stretch (430 frames). Flat
range images are unchanged: their depth is along the view axis.

Measured (forest flight, frame log, GTX 1060, the Mid-360's 3600 x
1047 panorama at 50 Hz, 1146 x 444 sub-cameras), against the previous
renderer: GPU per panorama 37.3 -> 33.6 ms by the discard, -> 27.7 ms
with the cull; 98.2 -> 77.6 M triangles and 43.5 k -> 33.8 k instances
per panorama; CPU 11.0 -> 9.5 ms; the flight 0.243x -> 0.315x real
time.
